<p>Travelers who spent time exploring Teruel's Mudéjar architecture and are continuing their Aragón itinerary — often toward a flight home or an onward high-speed rail connection — are the primary audience for this route. Because Teruel's public transport connections are relatively limited, this transfer is also a practical choice for anyone who simply wants a confirmed departure and arrival time rather than planning around a sparse regional timetable.</p>
